nodecode-otari is a rewrite of mozilla-ai's mozilla-ai/hermes-provider-otari:
https://github.com/mozilla-ai/hermes-provider-otari
commit 9d9ba9a55ddb713195d77d1931a4970769de7ae1
Apache-2.0, Copyright (c) 2026 Mozilla.ai (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the plugin's whole surface, which is one provider registration
(otari/__init__.py) — the gateway's base address, the OTARI_API_KEY key, the
OpenAI-compatible chat wire it speaks, and its reasoning-effort spelling
(otari/__init__.py:19-29: max sent as xhigh, a rung the gateway does not
accept left out). In their place the cell adds Otari's row to Nodecode's
models catalog, answers the credential from the same variable, and spells the
effort in the round's body; the models come from the gateway's own
GET /api/v1/models, which is where Nodecode's listing looks anyway.

Left out: Hermes's plugin manifest and registration API (plugin.yaml,
register_provider), which Nodecode cells replace with a declared section and
hooks; and the plugin's OTARI_BASE_URL environment variable, whose job the
section's base_url does. Nothing else of the original exists to leave out: it
ships no tools, hooks, commands, dependencies or bundled models.
